    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3489"
                            type="person">Dr. E. F. Curtz</rs>
                        <lb/>173 Broadway <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                            York</rs> 7, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N.
                        Y.</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-05-09">May 9, 1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3489" type="person">Dr.
                        Curtz</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>As I understand you have been kind enough to take interest in the career of my
                    friend and former assistant, <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2023" type="person"
                        >Dr. Hans Weil</rs>.</p>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2023" type="person">Hans Weil</rs>
                    since 1929 when I was Professor of Philosophy at the University of <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__143" type="place">Frankfurt a/M</rs>. <rs
                        ref="#tillich_person_id__2023" type="person">Dr. Weil</rs> was not only a
                    well-known writer but he was also regarded as one of the best young teachers at
                    the University in that time. He combines a great amount of creative thinking
                    with practical educational abilities. He was a good speaker, having overcome the
                    results of a childhood&apos;s accident with energy and passion for his work. </p>
                <p>I would be grateful if you would help him to find a place in the field of
                    education which, I believe, is his mission. I am sure he would do an excellent
                    job as he has done it not only in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__143" type="place"
                        >Frankfurt a/M</rs> but also in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__219"
                        type="place">Italy</rs> where he founded and headed his own school.</p>
                <p>I shall be happy to give you any further information you may desire.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours sincerely,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>
                        <lb/>Professor at Union Theological Seminary, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
